sunxi: display on request, with the Anbernic H700 panels

knulli boots every H700 board with one boot package; the panel is only
known from the board device tree picked after the first boot.
SUNXI_DISP_ON_DEMAND skips the display at board init; knulli_disp <dtb>
[<bmp>] points working_fdt at a board tree, brings its panel up and shows
the bmp, and at bootm the frame buffer is handed to the kernel disp node.
LCD_SUPPORT_ANBERNIC_H700 is the kernel panel driver of knulli linux patch
0004 (vendor init tables, bit-banged 3-wire SPI).

